---
import {directMeasure,mixedMeasure,financialRecord,money} from '../lib/data';
import SourceNote from './SourceNote.astro';
const ids=['apers_september_holding','atrs_february_purchase','atrs_january_funding'];
const labels=['APERS reported positions','ATRS completed bond purchase','ATRS manager funding, including its bond'];
---
<section class="composition" aria-labelledby="agency-by-agency" style="margin-top:0"><span class="eyebrow">Dates and definitions come first</span><h2 id="agency-by-agency">The pension record, agency by agency.</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Dated pension financial record"><table><caption class="sr-only">Pension observations and events; amounts cannot all be added together</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Amount</th><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Basis</th></tr></thead><tbody>{ids.map((id,i)=>{const r=financialRecord(id);return <tr><th scope="row">{labels[i]}</th><td>{money(r.amount)}</td><td>{r.effectiveDate}</td><td>{r.basis}</td></tr>})}</tbody></table></div><p style="margin-top:22px">The purchase and manager funding overlap. July later observes the ATRS bond; it does not add another purchase.</p><details class="transcript"><summary>How the cross-agency measures work</summary><p><strong>{money(directMeasure.amount)}: {directMeasure.label}.</strong> This adds Treasury’s dated $50 million derived residual, APERS’s $25 million reported positions, and ATRS’s $9.9 million purchase.</p><p style="margin-top:18px"><strong>{money(mixedMeasure.amount)}: {mixedMeasure.label}.</strong> This substitutes the full $50 million ATRS manager funding for its underlying bond. It is a different measure, not a securities holdings total.</p><p style="margin-top:18px">Both combine different record dates. Neither includes Treasury’s additional $10 million processing instruction. Neither establishes current same-day holdings.</p><SourceNote ids={directMeasure.sourceIds}/></details></section>
